WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.940
- [Tim Cook] Introducing Apple Vision Pro.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.540
Vision Pro. Vision Pro.
Vision Pro. Vision Pro.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.050
- Yes, Apple's mixed reality
headset is now a reality.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.150
Here at the company's Cupertino campus,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.750
it just showed off the
long-awaited reality headset.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.760
The face computer, my term not theirs,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.140
bridges virtual reality

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.660
where you're fully
transported to a virtual world

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.190
with augmented reality,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.010
where you see virtual
objects in your real world.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.060
Apple's calling it-

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.680
- Spatial computing.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.370
- [Joanna] And yes, it-
- [Tim Cook] Starts at $3499.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.980
- [Joanna] Apple spent 45
minutes detailing how it works

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.840
and what you can do with it.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.110
Let me break it down for
you in way less time.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.910
These are $3 lab goggles.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.590
The headset looks like a pair of aluminum

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.780
and glass ski goggles.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.950
Basically these, but cooler
and way more expensive.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.330
The front of the device has a screen

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.030
so people can see your eyes
when you're wearing it.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.590
Creepy, kinda.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.470
It looks way slimmer and
lighter than Meta's Quest Pro.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.790
One of the big reasons for that,

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.790
a cord from the headset
attaches to this battery pack.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.190
Apple says the battery
will last two hours.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.220
You can also plug it into
an outlet to use it all day.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.053
On the one hand,

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:11.340
I'm excited not to wear
a battery on my head.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.610
On the other hand, battery fanny packs.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.340
There are no controllers
like other VR headsets.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.500
You use your hands to navigate around.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.630
There are multiple
cameras on the device too,

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.100
which help you see the real world

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.780
with digital objects in it.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.790
The Apple Watch-like digital crown dial

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.230
lets you get to the home screen

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.837
and also controls how much
of the virtual world you see.

00:01:30.837 --> 00:01:32.130
You can even use the cameras

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.758
to capture spatial 3D videos and photos.

00:01:35.758 --> 00:01:37.620
- [Apple Spokesperson] It's
easy to capture a spatial photo

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.440
or video with just the press of a button.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.940
- [Joanna] If you're
wondering how you log in,

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.010
iris scans with Optic ID.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.160
Apple says your eye scans
are kept on the device.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.050
So what do you do once
you've got that on your head

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.880
and all that other stuff on your body?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.730
Well, Apple showed off a few experiences.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.350
Surprisingly, a lot of the things shown

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.850
have to do with work.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.121
You can see multiple windows
from your Mac above your desk.

00:02:00.121 --> 00:02:02.820
- [Apple Spokesperson]
Microsoft apps like Excel, Word,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.570
and Teams make full use
of the expansive canvas

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.720
and sharp text rendering of Vision Pro.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.970
- [Joanna] You can FaceTime
with family or colleagues.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.800
The FaceTime stuff is pretty crazy.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.470
Since you're not holding a
camera out in front of your face,

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.470
you create a scan instead,
basically a hologram,

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.210
to appear in your chats.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.860
There's stuff to do in your downtime too,

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.750
like watching immersive 3D movies

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.670
and playing Apple Arcade games.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.040
There's game controller support too.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.300
But what Apple's really hoping

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.760
is that software developers
build new applications

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.090
for VisionOS, the operating
system powering it all.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.290
Disney CEO Bob Iger

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.260
even showed off some
virtual Disney experiences.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.560
- This platform will allow us
to bring Disney to our fans

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.620
in ways that were previously impossible.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.180
- I have a lot of thoughts on it all.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.740
I should be trying it out soon.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.047
Stay tuned for my first impressions.

00:02:52.047 --> 00:02:54.630
(gentle music)

